From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:49:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Learner: profile settings for motor model and RLS
 forgetting factor

Make the two changes from 5bf60bd and f5d3392 selectable from the profile
instead of hardcoded:

- learner_simple_motor_model (0/1, default 1)
  1: omega - idle = a*d - tau*omegaDot (simplified model, f5d3392)
  0: omega = a*d + b*sqrt(d) + c - tau*omegaDot (full model, before f5d3392)
  Also applied in setFxRlsToProfile, so the in-flight reset initialises
  the motor RLS consistently with the selected model.

- learner_rls_lambda (0..1000000, lambda * 1e6, default 1000000)
  0: forgetting factor from the bandwidth equation in rlsInit
  otherwise: use the given value (clamped to [0.9, 1])
  rlsInit computes the equation again; the learner overrides it through
  the new rlsSetLambda. rlsInit has no callers outside the learner.

Defaults reproduce the current behaviour. learnerConfig PG version 1 -> 2.
Both settings are written to the blackbox header.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
